  "description": "Gates Carbon belt drive compatible\n\nBraze-ons for rear rack and fenders (disc brake-compatible racks only)\n\n1-1/8” size headtube (34mm ID)\n\nSizes: 46, 50, 52, 54, 56, 58. 60, 62 and 66cm (We recommend 650b tires on the 46cm)\n\n4.79 lbs (frame);\n\nThe original inspiration for the Wolverine was “monster cross”, but it is seriously so much more. Its geometry is stable enough for off road touring, but sporty enough for all-around adventure. With its sliding dropouts, you can turn it into a single-speed, run geared hubs like Rohloff, and of course you can still run deraileurs.. With a split seatstay, it is compatible with the Gates Carbon Belt Drive.\n\nThe primary differences between the 4.0 and 4.1 is that the frame and forks now fit the flat mount brake standard.\n\n(Also check out the Wolverine v.4.1 Type-A! See chart for their differences)\n\nTire Fit on size 50cm and up:\n\n​Tire Fit on size 46cm:",
